The image was convincing because it looked like what I expected to see. Reality is often less cooperative.

A real sky has an inconvenient wire running through it. A real conversation ends without finding its point. We learn to remove these things, then wonder why everything feels the same.

Perhaps the awkward details are not defects in the picture. Perhaps they are how the world lets us know it was there.
